WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.460
From method acting madness to weird food&nbsp;
choices to the place Johnny Galecki stuck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.960
all of his used chewing gum, these actors&nbsp;
had some seriously gross on-set habits.

00:00:10.273 --> 00:00:14.233
When Robert Pattinson landed the role of&nbsp;
Edward Cullen in the Twilight franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:17.640
he entered the realm of sudden&nbsp;
superstardom. He also developed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.468
a reputation for having poor hygiene. A&nbsp;
source on the set of New Moon told E! News,

00:00:22.468 --> 00:00:25.560
"He stinks. I mean, it's awful. He never showers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.438
and it drives people on the set&nbsp;
crazy. [...] He completely reeks."

00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:32.438
"P.U. It is ripe in here."

00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:36.180
Not everyone associated with Twilight&nbsp;
complained about Pattinson's smell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:38.357
Kristen Stewart told People,

00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:41.100
"He smells great. [...] It's kind of an animalist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.834
thing that goes on. It went along&nbsp;
with the movie, so it was perfect."

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:48.095
When Extra asked Pattinson about&nbsp;
not washing his hair for six weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.095 --> 00:00:50.280
Pattinson made a shocking admission, saying,

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:53.794
"If you don't care if your hair is clean&nbsp;
or not, then why would you wash it?"

00:00:53.794 --> 00:00:58.320
Not to worry — becoming a model for Dior&nbsp;
helped Pattinson clean up his act. In 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.760
he told The Wall Street Journal,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.240
"I can't tell if it's because of my&nbsp;
association with Dior or because I'm older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.960
but I've started moisturizing. It's been&nbsp;
a quite profound change in my life."

00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:10.398
His co-stars must appreciate him&nbsp;
arriving on set fresh and clean.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.940
Brad Pitt has long been a sex symbol.&nbsp;
He's been crowned People's Sexiest Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.844
Alive twice. But the star is also&nbsp;
famous for having poor hygiene.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.161
"Say it ain't so!"

00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:23.820
Pitt readily admits to not showering&nbsp;
regularly but insists baby wipes keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.612
him fresh. His Inglourious Basterds&nbsp;
co-star, Eli Roth, told People,

00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:31.500
"After a scene, Brad had to get next to me&nbsp;
for a close-up shot, and he said, 'Damn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.840
you're ripe.' I said, 'I didn't have time to&nbsp;
shower.' He said, 'Baby wipes, man, baby wipes.'"

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.460
Pitt also stopped using soap and antiperspirant&nbsp;
because of concerns for the environment and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:47.040
toxins the products contain, opting for a homemade&nbsp;
concoction. Not everyone was as impressed as Roth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.080
was with Pitt's hygiene hack. Even Pitt's children&nbsp;
have staged a mutiny over his insufficient bathing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.267
habits. If his family is complaining, can&nbsp;
you imagine what his co-stars have to say?

00:01:56.267 --> 00:02:01.620
Pitt isn't alone in his aversion to soap, bathing,&nbsp;
and deodorant. Many stars have come out in recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.840
years as being infrequent bathers. Mila Kunis and&nbsp;
Ashton Kutcher talked about their relaxed approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.180
to bathing with Dax Shepard on the Armchair Expert&nbsp;
podcast. And Jake Gyllenhaal told Vanity Fair,

00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:15.155
"More and more I find bathing&nbsp;
to be less necessary."

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.980
Shia LaBeouf doesn't claim to be a method&nbsp;
actor, but, while filming the war epic Fury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.000
the cast and crew were troubled by the&nbsp;
extreme methods he used to get into character.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.760
LaBeouf told Dazed Digital that after landing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.960
role he trained with the 41st Infantry&nbsp;
of the US National Guard. He admitted,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.660
"I pulled my tooth out, knifed my face up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.380
and spent days watching horses die.&nbsp;
I didn't bathe for four months."

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.040
"It seems wild 'cause it's a scar but&nbsp;
you get a lotta scars doing these things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.495
Moreso emotionally than the physical stuff.&nbsp;
That's really the smallest part of the job."

00:02:45.495 --> 00:02:47.115
A source told The Daily Mail,

00:02:47.115 --> 00:02:50.400
"Shia was warned about his&nbsp;
behavior by several people on set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.520
including Brad Pitt and director David Ayer."

00:02:53.696 --> 00:02:58.316
You read that right, even Pitt was offended&nbsp;
by LaBeouf's poor hygiene and self-mutilation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.316 --> 00:03:02.220
According to The Daily Mail, he even wound&nbsp;
up staying in a different lodging than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.720
the rest of the cast and crew because of&nbsp;
his poor hygiene and troubling behavior.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.920
Jim Carrey's bizarre and annoying antics on&nbsp;
the set of Man on the Moon were so strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.360
Universal didn't want any behind-the-scenes&nbsp;
footage released. In Chris Smith's Netflix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.473
documentary Jim &amp; Andy: The Great Beyond,&nbsp;
audiences saw this footage for the first time.

00:03:20.473 --> 00:03:22.856
"It's really weird. It's totally surreal."

00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:26.940
While making Miloš Forman's biopic about&nbsp;
the eccentric comedian Andy Kaufman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.320
Carrey got lost in the role, staying in&nbsp;
character on set for four months of filming.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.200
In the documentary, Carrey&nbsp;
says that when he got the role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.035
Kaufman's spirit tapped him&nbsp;
on the shoulder and took over.

00:03:37.152 --> 00:03:40.872
"What happened afterwards was out of my control."

00:03:40.872 --> 00:03:44.700
Carrey certainly seems possessed by&nbsp;
something, and it wasn't always fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.440
for the cast and crew. For example, Carrey&nbsp;
made everyone on set call him Andy — or Tony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.715
when Carrey inhabited Kaufman's&nbsp;
belligerent alter ego, Tony Clifton.

00:03:53.715 --> 00:03:58.320
He was combative and rude, especially with&nbsp;
Jerry Lawler, the professional wrestler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:03.300
who plays himself in the film, going so&nbsp;
far as to spit in his face. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.660
Carrey won a Golden Globe for his&nbsp;
performance, but for the cast and crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.620
Carrey's method acting was unprofessional&nbsp;
and disruptive to the production.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.500
In 2005, when Matthew McConaughey was named&nbsp;
People's Sexiest Man Alive, he told the world,

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.600
"I haven't worn deodorant in 20 years."

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.420
McConaughey's stance isn't&nbsp;
driven by health concerns;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:27.060
the actor just doesn't think it's necessary. In&nbsp;
a 2008 interview with Playboy, McConaughey said,

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.060
"The women in my life, including&nbsp;
my mother, have all said, 'Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:34.201
your natural smell smells, one, like&nbsp;
a man, and, two, smells like you.'"

00:04:34.201 --> 00:04:37.500
That is, until he worked with Kate&nbsp;
Hudson, who begged him to use her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.520
natural deodorant while filming Fool's&nbsp;
Gold. McConaughey explained to Playboy,

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.820
"She always brings a salt rock,&nbsp;
which is some natural deodorant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.920
and says, 'Would you please put this on?'"

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.140
Apparently, others have worked with McConaughey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.040
and found absolutely nothing offensive&nbsp;
about his smell. Yvette Nicole Brown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.480
who worked with the actor on Tropic Thunder, told&nbsp;
The Jess Cagle Show he actually smelled good.

00:04:57.617 --> 00:05:00.017
"He smells like granola and good livin'."

00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:04.920
It must have been extra hot in Australia while&nbsp;
filming Fool's Gold, or maybe McConaughey started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:09.120
taking multiple showers every day. Either way, he&nbsp;
and Hudson have made a couple of films together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.780
and they had great screen chemistry&nbsp;
— even if she thought he smelled bad.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.500
Shailene Woodley is known for being&nbsp;
health-conscious and into natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.820
healing and natural beauty products, but&nbsp;
one of her co-stars didn't appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.360
her herbalism. Miles Teller said he&nbsp;
hated kissing her while filming The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.400
Spectacular Now because her numerous herbal&nbsp;
tinctures tasted bad. Teller told Vulture,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:33.120
"She would take these herbal supplements,&nbsp;
these Chinese herbal supplements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.500
and they tasted like crap. And she would always&nbsp;
eat them right before we had a kissing scene!"

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:42.000
Woodley didn't enjoy shooting their kissing&nbsp;
scenes either. Reportedly she took issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.520
with Teller's breath, too. Woodley told Vulture,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.960
"We'd have to kiss in a scene, and he'd be like,&nbsp;
'Shay, you just ate dirt.' And I'd be like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.760
'Miles, you just ate licorice.' It&nbsp;
was just this ongoing back-and-forth."

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.780
"You stink."

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.140
"No, you stink."

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:02.040
This might surprise fans who have seen Woodley and&nbsp;
Teller in four films together. But don't worry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.420
this popular film duo are friends despite their&nbsp;
complaints about each other's on-set habits.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.420
Woodley also apparently loved&nbsp;
Teller's recent work in Top Gun:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.260
Maverick, telling People that Teller&nbsp;
is a, quote, "wildly talented actor."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.380
Although Teller appreciated the&nbsp;
praise, he told the publication,

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.460
"She certainly didn't have to do anything&nbsp;
publicly for me to know that she supports me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:24.000
and that we are really good friends. [...]&nbsp;
We've been very close for a long time."

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.720
Maybe next time they meet up to play&nbsp;
romantic leads, they can just agree on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:32.220
breath mints or a universally inoffensive&nbsp;
glass of water before kissing scenes.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:37.020
Word is Jennifer Lawrence, quote, "tortured" her&nbsp;
Hunger Games leading men by eating stinky food&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:40.380
before her kissing scenes with both&nbsp;
Liam Hemsworth and Josh Hutcherson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:44.880
and she didn't feel bad about it one bit.&nbsp;
Lawrence confirmed this on The Graham Norton Show.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.160
"Whenever I had to kiss Josh&nbsp;
and Liam for The Hunger Games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:52.080
who cares. I'd eat like mustard&nbsp;
and tuna — like who cares?"

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:54.540
Hemsworth had his chance to&nbsp;
complain about Lawrence's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.640
gross on-set food choices to Jimmy Fallon.

00:06:56.734 --> 00:07:00.514
"Anytime I had to kiss Jennifer was&nbsp;
pretty uncomfortable. Pretty awkward."

00:07:00.514 --> 00:07:03.900
When Fallon was baffled by this&nbsp;
declaration, Hemsworth explained,

00:07:03.998 --> 00:07:07.358
"She's one of my best friends. I love&nbsp;
her. But if we had a kissing scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.358 --> 00:07:10.080
she would make a point of&nbsp;
eating garlic or tuna fish."

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:14.280
Not to worry — these two are clearly friends&nbsp;
who enjoy giving each other a hard time.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:18.960
From stories that surfaced about the practical&nbsp;
jokes and pranks pulled during production of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.940
Hunger Games movies, it seems like Lawrence's food&nbsp;
choices were more of a joke than poor hygiene or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:29.160
a deliberate tactic to torment her leading men.&nbsp;
And the men occasionally fought back. Hutcherson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.180
once scared Lawrence so badly that she peed&nbsp;
her pants when he put a mutilated dummy in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:37.020
the bathroom of her trailer. If you're going to&nbsp;
dish it out, you'd better learn to take it, right?

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.820
Jason Segel was a smoker when he landed a&nbsp;
starring role on the hit series How I Met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:47.280
Your Mother. Reportedly, his co-star and on-screen&nbsp;
wife, Alyson Hannigan, told him she wouldn't do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.720
any kissing scenes with him because of his&nbsp;
smoker's breath. Hannigan told Digital Spy,

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.100
"I cannot stand cigarette smoke.&nbsp;
It's like kissing an ashtray and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.400
he's trying to be polite by having&nbsp;
gum or mints, but it doesn't help."

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.880
According to Hannigan, the pair&nbsp;
developed a system. She explained,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:06.060
"When we started the pilot he was&nbsp;
like, 'Get me to stop smoking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.240
I'll be your best friend'. So we&nbsp;
did this bet where he would owe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.560
me $10 every time he had a cigarette.&nbsp;
After the first day, he owed me $200.'"

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.280
Fortunately, Segel quit,&nbsp;
but it only lasted a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.260
after which stress got him started again.&nbsp;
But despite being grossed out by his smoking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:27.360
Hannigan loved working with Segal on the series.&nbsp;
She broke down crying while trying to explain why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:31.920
she would miss him during a cast reunion on The&nbsp;
Talk. And the feelings were obviously mutual.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:37.680
"Aly taught me a lot about how to be a man,&nbsp;
I gotta say. I was 25 when I took the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.920
and I think we've all been&nbsp;
through a lot personally."

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.280
It goes to show that just because&nbsp;
an actor has a gross on-set habit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.680
it doesn't mean their co-stars&nbsp;
won't grow to love them.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:51.840
Allegedly, Arnold Schwarzenegger intentionally&nbsp;
farted in the face of one of his co-stars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:56.460
Miriam Margolyes is probably best known for&nbsp;
playing Professor Sprout in Harry Potter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:01.560
Juliet's nurse in Baz Luhrmann's iconic film&nbsp;
Romeo + Juliet. Her hilarious and brutally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.300
honest answers to interview questions have made&nbsp;
her a popular and entertaining talk show guest.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.800
The British actor told I've Got News For You&nbsp;
that she didn't enjoy meeting Schwarzenegger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.520
while filming the horror movie End of Days,&nbsp;
and she hasn't gotten over it, saying,

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.480
"He's a bit too full of himself, and I don't&nbsp;
care for him at all. He's a Republican,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:23.580
which I don't like. He was actually quite rude.&nbsp;
He farted in my face. Now, I fart. Of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.140
I do — but I don't fart in people's faces.&nbsp;
He did it deliberately, right in my face."

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:33.000
Not only was this on-set behavior gross, but&nbsp;
Margolyes also found it offensive, saying,

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.320
"I was playing Satan's sister, and&nbsp;
he was killing me, so he had me in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.560
a position where I couldn't escape and&nbsp;
lying on the floor. And he just farted."

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.800
Despite Variety reaching out to&nbsp;
Schwarzenegger's representatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:47.040
for comment, it appears the actor&nbsp;
has never addressed her accusation.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:52.500
Johnny Galecki's unhygienic habit of disposing&nbsp;
of his gum on the set of The Big Bang Theory was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:57.000
so gross one of his co-stars couldn't resist&nbsp;
talking about it. If you're familiar with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.960
comedy series, you know the elevator in the&nbsp;
apartment building where Sheldon, Leonard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:06.300
and Penny lived remained out of order for years on&nbsp;
end. Kunal Nayyar, who played Raj Koothrappali on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:10.380
the series, revealed to Daily Express that&nbsp;
the on-set stairs led to nowhere, saying,

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:14.340
"There's a wall there where Johnny Galecki,&nbsp;
for 12 years, would stick his chewing gum on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.480
I'm not joking; there's a wall of 3,000&nbsp;
dried chewing gum from Johnny Galecki."

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.640
This is a totally gross on-set habit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.020
but do you know what's even more disgusting?&nbsp;
Some fans would probably spend a pretty penny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.620
to buy that wall of chewing gum as a&nbsp;
weird piece of celebrity memorabilia.

